{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/905729-cr\u00faac-high-level-rituals","id":905729,"title":"Cr\u00faac, High Level Rituals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-02T09:52:33-07:00","id":905729,"title":"Cr\u00faac, High Level Rituals","content":"Anyone created or used a level 6+ Cr\u00faac ritual? I am playing (and co-narrating) a game with elder vampires, one of character reach Cr\u00faac 6 and I need ideas about high level rituals.<br /> <br /> We are using the Vampire the Requiem Second Edition and the Blood Sorcery - Sacraments &amp; Blasphemies rules.<br /> <br /> Until now I converted a old level 5 ritual, Roving Hut, to level 6 using Blood Sorcery rules. I created a new one too: a ritual used to &quot;purge&quot; a bloodline from someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/437-shadowninja","name":"shadowninja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T10:04:50-07:00","id":905734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shadowninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/905729-cr\u00faac-high-level-rituals#post905729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone created or used a level 6+ Cr\u00faac ritual? I am playing (and co-narrating) a game with elder vampires, one of character reach Cr\u00faac 6 and I need ideas about high level rituals.<br /> <br /> We are using the Vampire the Requiem Second Edition and the Blood Sorcery - Sacraments &amp; Blasphemies rules.<br /> <br /> Until now I converted a old level 5 ritual, Roving Hut, to level 6 using Blood Sorcery rules. I created a new one too: a ritual used to &quot;purge&quot; a bloodline from someone.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If I'm not wrong, in second edition the maximum level of disciplines is 5. You can't go over 5. I don't like this change too but...it's written...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T10:14:56-07:00","id":905741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/905729-cr\u00faac-high-level-rituals?p=905734#post905734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If I'm not wrong, in second edition the maximum level of disciplines is 5. You can't go over 5. I don't like this change too but...it's written...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are not wrong. So I dont think the original poster will get much help for what dot 6 should be.<br /> <br /> I do recommend creating some sort of unique and fun devotion instead of &quot;level 6&quot; It lets you make more specialized characters instead of saying they have a 6th dot.. which does?? What?<br /> <br /> Unfortunately I do not have any advice on what a good devotion would be. Wish I could help more.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: also.. correct me if I am wrong.. but your humanity is capped by your cruac, so you could only have a 4 humanity and if you kept going with this, your vampire could get scary low... <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 06-02-2016, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T10:17:07-07:00","id":905745,"title":"","content":"Well, my game started before the Second Edition and we still using a few old rules and options, like Threnodies, Themes to Blood Sorcery and Devotions, all receiving adaptations.<br /> <br /> I don't find this information. The book don't say anything about this discipline limit, only say about attibutes and skills going beyond 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/437-shadowninja","name":"shadowninja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T10:40:18-07:00","id":905762,"title":"","content":"Well the only thing I remember in 1e core was a mention in the Bloodline section that a 6+ Cruac ritual could remove or change a bloodline potentially. Other than that, there were really no guidelines to get a good read on what it might be able to do. One GM we had just lifted the restrictions from the Blood Sorcery book (No spiritual realm interactions, no permanent effects, etc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T10:50:01-07:00","id":905771,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Requiem never had anything about &gt;5 disciplines. It's not explicitely written that it's not possible, but nothing exists to support the idea it would be possible. There are words on raising other attributes and skills to that level, but not disciplines or merits (although logically, merits like ressources could go beyong 5 given that 5 was described in WoD corebook as several million bucks).<br /> <br /> To further that point, look at the various NPC vampires stated in the books. The best example is Night Horror Immortal sinners. Some of them (rare, even vampires described as obescenely powerful like Unholy are kinda underpowered compared to what is said about them), who are really old and powerful have lots of high level disciplines, but none of them go beyond 5. The best example is Zagreus, the only really overpowered vampire NPC (barring the sightless mother, but she's a ghost), more than 2000 years old, BP9. He's got Auspex, Celerity, Dominate, Majesty and Vigor maxed out. With the new rules, he's got like 16 defense. But he doesn't have any discipline above 6. He has an overpowered devotion, though (and another one that requires knowing obfuscate, but whatever, some of those NPCs don't always make sense and it's easy to fix anyway).<br /> <br /> Devotions seem like a good compromise. The thing is some of them need you to reach a certain level of blood potency to be used, so they're effectively similar. For example, Zagreus' unique devotion requires BP7 or something.<br /> <br /> Then, you have bloodlines, that can develop very specialized disciplines, some of which can be pretty powerful, and then, you can make devotions with them. A good example is the prince of Budapest from the same book. His discipline allows him to influence the city he's in and he's developped a few devotions to go even beyond that.<br /> <br /> And then, I believe some devotions are combinations of disciplines AND sorcery (theban or cruac), so that could be a direction to take as well. Rafael Pope (again same book) has a devotion that uses both actually. Honestly, if you want ideas for big powers, I recommend reading Night Horror : Immortal Sinners. Most characters described in the book aren't that great or really usable in the long term, but some are pretty interesting (if only to steal some ideas and do your own thing) and the unique powers are pretty nice as reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T11:19:55-07:00","id":905794,"title":"","content":"I had an idea for Cruac of that Range once, came up with it as an intellectual exercise, Based on the Amanotsukai sect from the Circle of the Crone book.<br /> <br /> It Transmutes his blood into Sake that when he then consumes, extinguishes his hunger for blood until he chooses to sate it again, but he also cannot use disciplines during this time, though he is protected from the sun.<br /> <br /> Sound about right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T12:08:43-07:00","id":905838,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#263238\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><a href=\"http://www.google.com/url?q=http%3A%2F%2Fforum.theonyxpath.com%2Fforum%2Fmain-category%2Fmain-forum%2Fthe-new-world-of-darkness%2Fvampire-the-requiem%2F487155-are-there-6-dots-disciplines-ranks&amp;sa=D&amp;sntz=1&amp;usg=AFQjCNE0HWz2tKC6Cwa1z3CI3EgPttpUzQ\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/487155-are-there-6-dots-disciplines-ranks</a></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#263238\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><a href=\"http://www.google.com/url?q=http%3A%2F%2Fforum.theonyxpath.com%2Fforum%2Fmain-category%2Fmain-forum%2Fthe-new-world-of-darkness%2Fvampire-the-requiem%2F608558-disciplines-level-above-5&amp;sa=D&amp;sntz=1&amp;usg=AFQjCNFnzkfqI2hTtSRpKidx6D4PRey7OA\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5</a><br /> <br /> <br /> I cant quite recall, but I dont remember it being a thing in 1E either and the second link seems to go with that as well.<br /> <br /> It does say in the book in second edition disciplines are on a scale of 1-5. Which implies 6 doesnt exist. Like I ( and a few others have ) said a devotion would be a great step to take</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 06-02-2016, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T16:05:51-07:00","id":906033,"title":"","content":"In 1e this is somewhat relevant:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VtR 1e pg 114</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elders speak of mighty powers becoming available once a<br /> Kindred\u2019s Blood Potency reaches a certain degree. Levels one<br /> through five of a given Discipline always produce the listed<br /> effects, but some elders insist that once a vampire\u2019s potential<br /> with a Discipline reaches a certain point, she may break from<br /> the static incarnations of a given Discipline and manifest powers<br /> with her own personality invested in them. That is, mystic<br /> wisdom suggests that there is no hard-and-fast level-six<br /> power for Auspex, for example, and that a Kindred who masters<br /> Auspex at such a high level creates her own unique application.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also there is a sidebar pertaining to rituals in the bloodlines section:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VtR 1e pg 260</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">OPTION: A HOARY SECRET<br /> Theban Sorcery, the Coils of the Dragon and<br /> Cr\u00faac might include rituals that enable a Kindred<br /> to join or renounce a bloodline without the<br /> normal prohibitions or prerequisites. These rituals<br /> are immensely rare and obscure. Storytellers who<br /> wish to allow such false bloodline potential are<br /> advised to require exceedingly potent mastery of<br /> the various blood magics to perform them: rituals<br /> of level six, at the very least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then in Blood Sorcery: Sacraments and blasphemies a 6 dot threnody that requires Resilience 6:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blood Sorcery pg 50</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Truly Unfettered (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T23:42:58-07:00","id":906255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/905729-cr\u00faac-high-level-rituals?p=905741#post905741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You are not wrong. So I dont think the original poster will get much help for what dot 6 should be.<br /> <br /> I do recommend creating some sort of unique and fun devotion instead of &quot;level 6&quot; It lets you make more specialized characters instead of saying they have a 6th dot.. which does?? What?<br /> <br /> Unfortunately I do not have any advice on what a good devotion would be. Wish I could help more.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: also.. correct me if I am wrong.. but your humanity is capped by your cruac, so you could only have a 4 humanity and if you kept going with this, your vampire could get scary low...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Your humanity is capped by 10 - cruac dots, capping it at your cruac would mean learning a single dot of cruac would immediately cause an acolyte to drop to near draugrhood and only be able to raise humanity by buying more cruac first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T05:13:23-07:00","id":906327,"title":"","content":"<b>I got an idea:</b><br /> <br /> A ritual that let's you physically assume Garou form by wearing the skin of a Werewolf ? I got the idea from old stories about witches using a similar methods.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not sure you can really create Devotions from Cruac, since it's a school of magic, rather than a specific list of powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-03-2016, 08:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T09:44:47-07:00","id":906482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/905729-cr\u00faac-high-level-rituals?p=906255#post906255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Your humanity is capped by 10 - cruac dots, capping it at your cruac would mean learning a single dot of cruac would immediately cause an acolyte to drop to near draugrhood and only be able to raise humanity by buying more cruac first.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> yup do the math on what wrote. This thread is about 6 cruac, so the best humanity they could have is 4.. 10-cruac 6 is 4 like I said. There is still a cap on your humanity due to your cruac.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T09:44:51-07:00","id":906483,"title":"","content":"I believe the Elder book in development had an outline released where it mentioned Elders DO have unique rituals and such, even if not technically level 6+ if it meshes with earlier claims by developers. So, you might have something like &quot;Cruac 5, Prerequisite: BP6/7/etc&quot; rituals instead that serve the same purpose, or however that might work.<br /> <br /> That being said, my basic advice is look at level 5 rituals and how they're limited, then remove that limitation or make the base effect even stronger. Something like As One from 1st edition, for instance; make a level 6 version (Or Level 5, BP6, depending how it works) that requires no special sacrifices, just allows you to take on that 'god' form with a simple casting in one spot, and affects the entirety of a city (Or equivalent area). As others have mentioned, removing the Blood Sorcery limits also works; add versions of other rituals that work permanently now, or that affect other realms, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 06-03-2016, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T13:54:19-07:00","id":906686,"title":"","content":"1E VtR Blood Potency chart specifically listed Attributes, Skills, and Disciplines as what increased above 5. 2E VtR Blood Potency chart has omitted Disciplines. Devotions can mimic what would have been 6+ level powers, given enough dots (take a look at any of the examples in the main book as well as the old supplements).<br /> <br /> I agree with falco1029 that Elder powers will/should require BP level, not 6+ in a Discipline. There are examples of this in Ancient Mysteries. Personally, I hope they do away with Elder only power. I like the way everything scales in VtR, and all that Blood Potency does is determine Blood Pool/ Points a Turn, and maximum Attributes and Skills (I'd even be cool with dropping Skills, but meh).<br /> <br /> That being said, a house rule I thought of but never played out was that once a vampire achieved 6+ in a Discipline, it gave access to Devotions equal to their Discipline level -5. Admittedly, this was when XP costs increased with level, so it made sense to me that someone who spent 150 XP on dots 6-9 of in-clan Protean got access to any Devotions of Protean 1-4 (9-5=4).<br /> <br /> Essentially, given enough time and XP, Elders could have access to all kinds of Devotions, so long as they met the prerequisite Discipline level(s). This might not pan out well though with the new flat cost rates per level of a power. So...<br /> <br /> Something else I thought of was rather than individual powers, each level made it easier to use the Discipline (for all Disciplines except Celerity, Protean, Resilience, Vigor):<br /> <br /> 6: gain rule of 9 again<br /> 7: ignore up to 2 points of penalties<br /> 8: gain rule of 8 again<br /> 9: ignore up to 5 points of penalties<br /> 10: Plot Device, so long as vampire has a blood point can do anything Storyteller needs within Discipline's scope<br /> <br /> Celerity, Resilience, Vigor just continue to do what they do. Protean I had increase the amount of time required before Torpor dropped Blood Potency, but now that you no longer lose 6+, this seems kinda blah. Still, if any of this can provide ideas, cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T16:06:29-07:00","id":906771,"title":"","content":"Damn, I had misread that last part. Dropping blood potency doesn't reduce your attributes/skills anymore, very interesting.<br /> <br /> After thinking about it a little, I'm thinking more and more that 6+ disciplines are unnecessary. If you want to give elders more powers reflecting their total mstery of disciplines, devotions seem like the best choice. There are only so many basic disciplines you can use (before you turn to bloodlines), but a LOT of potential devotions if it's just a matter of matching a certain level of a certain discipline with another. Between two five dots disciplines, that would mean like 25 devotions (I'm not counting devotions that only require one discipline like conditioning, that would add to 35 in total). I'm not going to count how many devotions that means for all basic disciplines, but that's more than enough shit for an ancient vampire to study during all those years and enough unusual powers to confuse younger vampires and make them wonder what is even happening.<br /> <br /> Seriously, a few sessions ago, I put an unarmed Zagreus (from Night Horror : Immortal Sinners) up against one of my players whose character is almost entirely optimized for combat and an absolute beast considering his BP of only 2 (routinely throws like 20 dice before substracting defense, has a nerfed professionnal training and the kindred dueling merit and now owns a riot gear). He didn't know who Zagreus was and tried to stop him from leaving a room. Due to Zagreus' 16 defense, he only threw ' dice and missed (granted, he would have hurt him if he had hit even with 1 success), then Zagreus rolled well and punched him for like 20 bashing or something and put him into torpor on the spot. (Zagreus has 14 dice of raw brawl with vigor and he can spend 10 Vitae/turn and let's not even talk if he frenzies).<br /> <br /> It's ridiculous, and frankly, in a stand up fight between elders, they can put so much hurt it kind of boils down to who gets initiative first. It is my opinion that Unholy (from the same book) is ridiculously underpowered compared to how much hype she gets from all the books. Stat-wise, Zagreus crushes,her, but With lethal damage claws and enough vitae buff, she can just one-shot him regardless if she acts first (and she has maxed resilience so she would probably tank his first attack if he doesn't have kindred dueling 3 which didn't exist at the time of the book, but a kindred that old really should know how to seriously hurt another vampire by now).<br /> <br /> Now, let's consider that Zagreus isn't really a fight oriented elder. He's really a social character, but when you're that old you learn to crush idiots by default. His social skills and disciplines are so high he can basically do whatever he wants in a city populated by your average kindred without having to fight anyone himself. And I'm not even counting his devotion that lets him basically dominate fate. I mean, yeah, I guess he could be even more overpowered but are your characters really gonna get to a level where they can individually say &quot;Yeah, it's cool I can take him&quot; ? Unless they completely min/max to have the most ungodly killing machine of a character imaginable, I'd guess probably not.<br /> <br /> So yeah, make a zagreus-level NPC, dump a truckload of devotions on him and you've got pretty much an unbeatable blood god on your hands. Creatures more powerful than that would be beyond the potential reach of all but a commando of fully geared and XP'd to death PCs and at this point, it's probably a better idea to make a campaign out of finding some hidden weakness or artifact to exploit than actually go up to the ancient and try to punch him in the face.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Edit : No, no actually Unholy wrecks Zagreus in fisticuffs, mostly thanks to resilience. Damn, that discipline is beast (used to be the lamest of all, too), between the extra HP and the one turn armor for a point of vitae. That and doing lethal with the +2 claws, which is always nice. She's deceptively strong in the end. She sucks everywhere else, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","user":"S. Brechen","date":". 06-06-2016, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T13:58:49-07:00","id":913640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/905729-cr\u00faac-high-level-rituals?p=906771#post906771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After thinking about it a little, I'm thinking more and more that 6+ disciplines are unnecessary. If you want to give elders more powers reflecting their total mstery of disciplines, devotions seem like the best choice. There are only so many basic disciplines you can use (before you turn to bloodlines), but a LOT of potential devotions if it's just a matter of matching a certain level of a certain discipline with another. Between two five dots disciplines, that would mean like 25 devotions (I'm not counting devotions that only require one discipline like conditioning, that would add to 35 in total). I'm not going to count how many devotions that means for all basic disciplines, but that's more than enough shit for an ancient vampire to study during all those years and enough unusual powers to confuse younger vampires and make them wonder what is even happening.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with some math here... You imply that there's only one devotion for every discipline combination. However, you can have an infinite number of devotions with the same discipline requirements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T15:03:24-07:00","id":913677,"title":"","content":"True enough, I didn't take that into account, 35 would be a bare minimum then, but the point is pretty much the same. There's a boatload of potential devotions that a really old vampire could know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}